# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Cloudflare evaluates _redirects BEFORE serving static assets (unlike Netlify),
# so a naked `/* / 302` rule would catch even `/` and loop on itself.
# Pin every known path with a 200 rewrite first so they bypass any wildcard.
#
# Note (2026-05-22): a splat catch-all (`/*  /  302`) was tried for unknown
# paths but Cloudflare Pages returns 404 before evaluating it. Unknown paths
# are handled by 404.html (client-side replace to /) instead. When adding a
# new page, add a matching rewrite line below and rerun seo-consistency-check.

/             /index.html          200
/about        /about/index.html    200
/about/       /about/index.html    200
/privacy      /privacy/index.html  200
/privacy/     /privacy/index.html  200
/terms        /terms/index.html    200
/terms/       /terms/index.html    200
/favicon.svg  /favicon.svg         200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml         200
/robots.txt   /robots.txt          200
